# =====================================================================
# MIT reactor (Li filter) neutron beam (GPS). Geometry common to both beam macros:
#   - Incident from the top, travelling along -z (GPS default direction).
#   - 12 cm diameter disc, uniform in area (clinical aperture 12-14 cm).
#   - Source plane 1 cm above the phantom's top surface:
#       z = 11 cm for phantomType 0 (sphere, R 10) and 1 (cylinder, top z 10).
#       For the Snyder heads (top at z = 8.5 cm) change the centre to 9.5 cm.
#   - Angular spread: cosine law, 0-15 deg from the beam axis.
# Only the energy spectrum differs between the beam macros.
# See docs/GEOMETRY_AND_BEAMS.md.
# Source of spectrum: Mirzaei et al 2014 (MIT reactor beam with Li filter, mainly epithermal neutron source for BNCT), https://doi.org/10.1007/s10967-014-3397-2
# =====================================================================
/gps/particle neutron
/gps/pos/type Plane
/gps/pos/shape Circle
/gps/pos/centre 0. 0. 11. cm
/gps/pos/radius 6. cm
/gps/ang/type cos
/gps/ang/mintheta 0 deg
/gps/ang/maxtheta 15 deg
/gps/ang/minphi 0 deg
/gps/ang/maxphi 360 deg

# Energy spectrum digitised from the cited figure (docs/GEOMETRY_AND_BEAMS.md,
# section 3). Each weight is
# the probability of the interval ENDING at its energy; the first point is the lower edge.
/gps/ene/type User
/gps/hist/type energy
/gps/hist/point 1.559553e-06 0
/gps/hist/point 1.636440e-06 1.096149e-04
/gps/hist/point 1.717117e-06 1.096149e-04
/gps/hist/point 1.801773e-06 1.096149e-04
